icult  to get a man to  understand something but his salary  depends on not understanding it  the result can be an entire society  twisted to serve the interest  of its most powerful group we can also  compare it to someone like  cheryl sandberg who wanted to offer a  win-win solution to sexism by  encouraging women to  lean in of course serious scholars cudi  included  understand that these problems are far  too complicated to have any quick fixes  but complexity is not what the ideas  industry is interested in  cuddy isn't getting into the door at the  coca-cola center for civil and human  rights  which is a real thing by asking hard  questions about why union leaders in  their south american bottling plants  have repeatedly disappeared but she  might get a fat check for explaining to  their head of progress how workers can  personally grow  by feeling more confident cudi is an  interesting example precisely because  she seems acutely aware of these  problems becoming a fascinating subject  for gerhardis book to document  but cuddy's introspection is not  universally present in the many thought  leaders speaking to anyone who can cut a  50 grand check  and make no mistake that's really how  much some of them get paid  historian niall ferguson reportedly  received 50 to 75 000  per speech malcolm gladwell also  reportedly receives over 50 000  per speech and if you were mad that  hillary clinton was getting 200 grand to  speak to a bunch of wall street execs  it's common practice  for tons of politicians including every  ex-president like george w bush and bill  clinton  with the rare exception of jimmy carter  it's not that every idea any of these  people ever had is bad  while we might say hey get paid who  cares  it creates a perverse incentive for  intellectuals and ex-politicians to not  rock the boat too hard  unless they want to miss out on hundreds  of thousands of dollars this incentive  also creates an echo chamber of ideas  paid for and consumed by  the 